stprandial/PP) Target: Should be below 140 mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) at 2 hours after the start of a meal. Levels between 140–199 mg/dL indicate prediabetes, and 200 mg/dL or higher indicate diabetes.", "reference_indexes": [1, 2, 4, 5]}, {"snippet": "HbA1c Target: Normal is below 5.7%; 5.7%–6.4% indicates prediabetes; 6.5% or higher indicates diabetes.", "reference_indexes": [2, 6]}, {"snippet": "Special Considerations: South Asian populations often develop insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes at lower body mass indices (BMIs) and earlier ages compared to Western populations, making routine dual-testing (fasting blood sugar paired with a 2-hour postprandial test) common practice among Indian diabetologists."}], "reference_indexes": [0, 3, 4]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "You can read more about tracking and managing guidelines via health resources like Apollo 24|7 or Curelo Health .", "snippet_links": [{"text": "Apollo 24|7", "link": "https://www.apollo247.com/health-topics/general-medical-consultation/normal-range-for-fasting-blood-sugar-levels"}, {"text": "Curelo Health", "link": "https://curelohealth.com/blog/normal-blood-sugar-level"}], "reference_indexes": [0, 2]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"}, {"type": "list", "list": [{"snippet": "Are you looking at a specific lab report or self-test result?"}, {"snippet": "Are there any symptoms like increased thirst or fatigue?"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "I can help explain the numbers further."}], "references": [{"index": 0, "title": "Normal Range for Fasting Blood Sugar Levels", "link": "https://www.apollo247.com/health-topics/general-medical-consultation/normal-range-for-fasting-blood-sugar-levels", "snippet": "The normal range for fasting blood sugar levels is: * Normal: 70–99 mg/dL * Prediabetes (impaired fasting glucose): 100–125 mg/dL * Diabetes: 126 mg/dL or higher o...", "source": "Apollo 24|7", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.ap